**Ethical Hacking Exercise: Buffer Overflow Exploit**

**Scenario:** A fictional web application, "E-Commerce Portal" (ECP), has a vulnerable version of the `gets()` function. Our goal is to demonstrate a buffer overflow exploit and illustrate defensive strategies to prevent such attacks.

**Simulated Environment:** A Linux-based virtual machine (VM) with a vulnerable version of the `libc` library installed.

**Exploit Code:**
```c
// buffer_overflow_exploit.c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    char buffer[10];
    printf("Enter your input: ");
    gets(buffer); // Vulnerable function: gets()

    // Injection vector: overflow the buffer with malicious code
    char inject[] = "AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\x00\x0c\x3a\x72\x65\x74\x75\x72\x6d\x00\x2f\x62\x69\x6e\x2f\x73\x68\x00";
    printf("Injected payload: %s\n", inject);

    // Attempt to execute the injected payload
    system(inject);
    return 0;
}
```
**Compiling the Exploit Code:**
```bash
$ gcc -o buffer_overflow_exploit buffer_overflow_exploit.c
```
**Running the Exploit:**
```bash
$ ./buffer_overflow_exploit
